# Machine-specific git config — work email, private hosts, per-machine tweaks.
#
# `make link` copies this template to `config/git/config.untracked` on a fresh
# machine, and ONLY if that file doesn't exist yet (an existing one is never
# overwritten). That copy is git-ignored, so anything you put in it — including
# secrets — is NEVER committed. Edit the copy, not this template.
#
# The copy is pulled in by the [include] at the end of ./config and loaded
# AFTER it, so any value set here overrides the tracked config. Uncomment and
# adjust what you need:

# [user]
# 	email = me@work-company.com
